BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:iwaenc2026-20@iwaenc2026.org
DTSTAMP:20260824T220153Z
DTSTART:20260908T163000Z
DTEND:20260908T180000Z
SUMMARY:Cremona Guided Tour
DESCRIPTION:Starting from the Politecnico campus of Cremona\, housed in the former Manfredini barracks\, this guided walking tour invites participants on a gentle journey into the soul of the city. Step by step\, the atmosphere shifts from the quiet charm of the academic setting to the vibrant pulse of Cremona’s historic center\, revealing a landscape where past and present blend seamlessly. As the streets unfold\, each corner hints at centuries of stories\, craftsmanship\, and culture\, creating a sense of discovery that goes beyond what is seen. The walk becomes an experience of connection—between places\, people\, and traditions—leading participants toward the heart of the city in a relaxed and evocative atmosphere. More than a simple route\, this tour is an invitation to feel Cremona: to absorb its rhythm\, its elegance\, and its timeless spirit\, as the city gradually reveals itself along the way. Included in the registration fee.
URL:https://iwaenc2026.org/attend/social-program/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:iwaenc2026-21@iwaenc2026.org
DTSTAMP:20260824T220153Z
DTSTART:20260908T180000Z
DTEND:20260908T210000Z
SUMMARY:Dinner @ Juliette
DESCRIPTION:Shuttle bus from Cremona center right after the guided tour. Set in the elegant and intimate atmosphere of Juliette in Cremona\, this exclusive dinner offers a moment of refined conviviality reserved for conference participants. Guests will be welcomed into a dedicated space\, thoughtfully arranged to create a warm and engaging setting\, where conversation and connection can unfold naturally. The evening will be enriched by live musical entertainment\, adding a subtle yet captivating soundtrack that enhances the ambiance and reflects the city’s deep-rooted musical heritage. Each moment is designed to evoke a sense of harmony—between taste\, sound\, and shared experience. To ensure a seamless experience\, a dedicated shuttle service will be available for both the outward and return journeys from Cremona’s city center\, allowing participants to fully relax and enjoy the evening from beginning to end. Tickets available during the registration.
URL:https://iwaenc2026.org/attend/social-program/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:iwaenc2026-22@iwaenc2026.org
DTSTAMP:20260824T220153Z
DTSTART:20260909T063000Z
DTEND:20260909T073000Z
SUMMARY:Keynote 2 - Organizing the Acoustic World: Computational Principles of Auditory Attention
DESCRIPTION:The ability to navigate complex acoustic environments depends on more than recognizing sounds. It requires identifying what is behaviorally relevant\, organizing sensory inputs into meaningful objects\, and adapting to changing goals and contexts. This talk will examine the computational principles that support these abilities\, drawing on studies of auditory attention\, predictive processing\, and auditory scene analysis. I will present behavioral and neural evidence illustrating how top-down goals\, statistical learning\, and bottom-up organization interact to shape auditory representations and guide selective listening in natural acoustic scenes. I will conclude by discussing how these same principles are beginning to influence modern audio systems\, offering opportunities for closer integration between auditory neuroscience and machine listening.
URL:day_3.html#all
END:VEVENT
